"context": "Account 123456789012, region us-east-1. READ-ONLY work only. Service Quotas list_service_quotas for ServiceCode 'bedrock' returns only ~19 items per page regardless of MaxResults and a long NextToken, so you must paginate manually (pass NextToken as a string, never null) until exhausted, using a JMESPath filter such as Quotas[?contains(QuotaName,'Sonnet 5')] to keep output small (also try 'Sonnet-5', 'Sonnet 5.0', 'Claude Sonnet 5'). The right quota is the 'Cross-region model inference tokens per minute for Anthropic Claude Sonnet 5' type (the 'us.' profile = geographic cross-region, NOT 'Global cross-region' which applies to 'global.' profiles). get_service_quota on the quota code returns the applied value (list_service_quotas returns applied values by default; also compare with list_aws_default_service_quotas to report default vs applied, and check list_requested_service_quota_change_history_by_quota for pending/recent increases). If you can't find a Sonnet 5 TPM quota, say exactly which similar quotas exist and don't guess.\nFor usage: use CloudWatch namespace AWS/Bedrock, dimension ModelId = the us. inference profile id (discover with list_metrics / bedrock list_inference_profiles; likely 'us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-...'). Prefer the metric EstimatedTPMQuotaUsage if available (it already reflects quota burndown); otherwise compute quota-counted tokens per minute = InputTokenCount + CacheWriteInputTokenCount + (burndown multiplier x OutputTokenCount) -- verify the output-token burndown rate for this model in AWS docs (verify_aws_claim; for many recent Claude models it is 5x) and state which formula you used. Use Sum with 60s period over the last 15 days (ending now, 2026-11-23T21:15Z; chunk GetMetricData calls to stay under 100,800 datapoints per call). Note CloudWatch 1-minute resolution retention is 15 days, so report if the full window isn't available at 60s. Find the peak minute (timestamp UTC), its quota-counted tokens, headroom = quota - peak (absolute and %), and also the top 3 peak minutes and peak raw input/output tokens separately. Also report whether any InvocationThrottles occurred for that model in the window. Also check whether usage might appear under other ModelId dimension values (e.g., foundation-model id or other region profiles) and mention it if so.",
"timeframe": "2026-11-08T21:15:00Z to 2026-11-23T21:15:00Z",
"criteria": "Return concise: quota code + name, applied value vs default, peak minute + value, headroom, formula used, caveats."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Look up Sonnet 5 TPM quota and 15-day peak usage"}], "created_at": null}

